---
// counterfeit/index 1110 V5.astro
// V5 (Counterfeit Section Load 1110 V1): StackUpIndex (the four religion
// overviews, then the 25 How the Five Religions Stack Up sets) sits between the
// By the Numbers panel and the closing line.
// V4 (Etsy Handoff Counterfeit Restructure 1105 V4): the front door. The opening
// text of the retired /counterfeit/five-world-religions page, then the five
// religions as tiles (one row of five at every width; under 640px each shrinks to
// symbol, name, Enter), then the full-width By the Numbers panel for the growth
// page, then the page's closing line. No study cards: every tile opens its hub.
// Tiles, counts and hubs come from src/data/counterfeit.js. The h1 stays
// "Counterfeit" (the nav label and the section name; the mockup's "The Five Major
// World Religions" sits under it as the subtitle line).
// V3: The Serpent King joined the Buddhism group. V2: cards in GROUPS.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ReligionSymbol from '../../components/counterfeit/ReligionSymbol.astro';
import StackUpIndex from '../../components/stackup/StackUpIndex.astro';
import { RELIGIONS, countLine, hubHref } from '../../data/counterfeit.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Counterfeit | Nazaryah"
  description="The world's religions taken one at a time, from their own writings, and set beside Scripture: what each kept of the truth, and where it turned."
>
  <div class="cfx">
    <div class="cfx-wrap">
      <h1>Counterfeit</h1>
      <p class="cfx-sub">The Five Major World Religions</p>
      <p class="cfx-deck">Truth kept, then turned sideways.</p>

      <section class="cfx-intro">
        <p>A counterfeit only works when it looks like the real thing. No one prints a bill that resembles nothing; the closer the copy runs to the genuine, the easier it spends. The five largest religions on earth each hold pieces of truth that trace back to the Word, and each one turns those pieces sideways.</p>
        <p>Scripture explains why the pieces are there at all. Every nation descends from the sons of Noah (Genesis 10:32; Acts 17:26), and every nation once knew the Creator. Paul says they knew Him, yet "glorified him not as God" and traded His glory for images (Romans 1:21-23). What remained was a memory of the truth with the Root cut away. Even then, the work of the Law stayed written in the conscience (Romans 2:14-15), which is why so much of what these religions teach sounds familiar.</p>
        <p>Each study in this section takes one religion on its own terms, from its own writings, and sets it beside Scripture: what it kept, where it came from, and where it turned. Christianity stands last on purpose. By the time a reader reaches it, the pattern will already be familiar.</p>
      </section>

      <nav class="rels" aria-label="The five religions">
        {RELIGIONS.map((r) => (
          <a class="rel" href={hubHref(r.id)}>
            <ReligionSymbol id={r.id} uid={`tile-${r.id}`} />
            <div>
              <h3>{r.name}</h3>
              <p>{r.tile}</p>
              <span class="count">{countLine(r.id)}</span><br />
              <span class="enter">Enter →</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </nav>
      <p class="cfx-note">Follower counts are for 2026 (World Christian Database).</p>

      <a class="numbers" href="/counterfeit/five-world-religions/growth">
        <div class="numtext">
          <p class="kicker">By the Numbers</p>
          <h2>How They Have Grown</h2>
          <p>The world has grown more than five times over since 1900. The record shows which religions kept pace, which outran it, and which fell behind.</p>
          <ul class="hl">
            <li><b>Islam</b> doubled its share of the world, from 12.4% to 25.4%.</li>
            <li><b>Christianity</b> is still the largest, yet slipped from 34.5% to 32.2%.</li>
            <li><b>Judaism</b> fell from 0.7% to 0.2% while its numbers barely moved.</li>
          </ul>
          <span class="enter big">See the full record: two charts and the story behind them →</span>
        </div>
        <svg class="spark" viewBox="0 0 520 220" role="img" aria-label="Share of world population by religion, 1900 to 2026"><line x1="34" x2="402" y1="196.0" y2="196.0" stroke="#ece9e0"/><text x="28" y="200.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">0%</text><line x1="34" x2="402" y1="149.5" y2="149.5" stroke="#ece9e0"/><text x="28" y="153.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">10%</text><line x1="34" x2="402" y1="103.0" y2="103.0" stroke="#ece9e0"/><text x="28" y="107.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">20%</text><line x1="34" x2="402" y1="56.5" y2="56.5" stroke="#ece9e0"/><text x="28" y="60.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">30%</text><line x1="34" x2="402" y1="10.0" y2="10.0" stroke="#ece9e0"/><text x="28" y="14.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">40%</text><text x="34.0" y="214" text-anchor="start" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">1900</text><text x="402.0" y="214" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill="#8a8f99">2026</text><path d="M34.0,35.7 L238.4,42.1 L326.1,45.8 L384.5,47.1 L402.0,46.2" fill="none" stroke="#2a78d6" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="408.0" y="50.2" font-size="11" fill="#222">Christianity 32.2%</text><path d="M34.0,138.5 L238.4,123.4 L326.1,97.2 L384.5,82.9 L402.0,78.1" fill="none" stroke="#eb6834" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="408.0" y="82.1" font-size="11" fill="#222">Islam 25.4%</text><path d="M34.0,137.7 L238.4,138.6 L326.1,132.5 L384.5,131.3 L402.0,131.7" fill="none" stroke="#1baf7a" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="408.0" y="135.7" font-size="11" fill="#222">Hinduism 13.8%</text><path d="M34.0,159.6 L238.4,166.5 L326.1,162.2 L384.5,164.9 L402.0,166.0" fill="none" stroke="#eda100" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="408.0" y="170.0" font-size="11" fill="#222">Buddhism 6.5%</text><path d="M34.0,192.6 L238.4,194.2 L326.1,195.0 L384.5,195.1 L402.0,195.1" fill="none" stroke="#e87ba4" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><text x="408.0" y="199.1" font-size="11" fill="#222">Judaism 0.2%</text></svg>
      </a>

      <div class="su cfx-su"><StackUpIndex more /></div>

      <p class="cfx-close">Revelation names the people who come through every counterfeit standing: those who keep the commandments of Yahuah and hold to the belief of Yahushua (Revelation 14:12). Nothing kept back, and nothing turned sideways.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cfx {
    --navy: #1F3864;
    --ink: #222;
    --muted: #5a5f6b;
    --gold: #B8902F;
    --paper: #fdfcf8;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --line: #e4e0d4;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cfx *, .cfx *::before, .cfx *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  /* The site's global headings are Cinzel; this page's headings keep its own serif. */
  .cfx h1, .cfx h2, .cfx h3 { font-family: inherit; }
  .cfx-wrap { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 16px 48px; }
  .cfx h1 { color: var(--navy); font-size: 2.2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 6px; font-weight: normal; }
  .cfx-sub { font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--gold); font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 2px; }
  .cfx-deck { font-style: italic; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .cfx-intro p { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 760px; }
  .cfx-note { font-size: .88rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 10px 0 0; }

  /* Religion tiles (.rels, from the mockup): one row of five at every width. */
  .rels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .rel {
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 4px solid var(--navy); border-radius: 6px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; gap: 8px; padding: 16px 10px;
    text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); transition: transform .2s ease;
  }
  .rel:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); }
  .rel svg { width: 48px; height: 48px; flex: none; }
  .rel h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--navy); font-weight: normal; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .rel p { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .count { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--gold); font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .enter { color: var(--navy); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold); font-size: .95rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .rels { gap: 6px; }
    .rel { padding: 10px 4px; gap: 4px; }
    .rel svg { width: 34px; height: 34px; }
    .rel h3 { font-size: .68rem; line-height: 1.2; hyphens: auto; -webkit-hyphens: auto; }
    .rel p, .rel .count, .rel br { display: none; }
    .rel .enter { font-size: .7rem; }
  }

  /* By the Numbers panel */
  .numbers {
    margin-top: 28px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.15fr; gap: 24px; align-items: center;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 4px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 6px; padding: 24px;
    text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .numbers .kicker { font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--gold); font-size: .95rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .numbers h2 { color: var(--navy); font-weight: normal; font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .numbers p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .hl { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 18px; }
  .hl li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .hl b { color: var(--navy); font-weight: normal; }
  .enter.big { font-size: 1rem; }
  .spark { width: 100%; height: auto; font-family: Georgia, serif; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .numbers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .cfx-su { background: transparent; }
  .cfx-close { max-width: 760px; margin: 40px 0 0; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .cfx h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; } }
</style>
